IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-dates`

-- Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022 (Vic) -- the rules.
--
-- Parts 2 to 4 (eligibility, applying, deciding, paying, review, variation, repayment), the s 72 indexation and the
-- Part 7 transitional provisions a person with an old Tribunal award or an old act of violence meets. The victim's
-- questions are in voc-seat.l4, which imports this module and never restates a rule.
--
-- Answers follow the rulings on negatives (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE where the text itself says no, NOTHING (with a
-- NOTHING-kind tag) where it does not answer. The scheme decision maker's satisfactions, opinions and determinations are
-- facts given to the rules, never guessed.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Victims of Crime
-- (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022, Version No. 002 (1 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of
-- Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced
-- except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
-- (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a `and` b MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a `and` b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

-- Nothing below zero.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` a MEANS `the greater of` a `and` 0

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions (s 3)`

-- s 3(1) "relevant offence means any of the following -- (a) an offence punishable by imprisonment that involves assault
-- on, or injury or threat of injury to, a person; (b) an offence against Subdivision (8A) ... (8FA) of Division 1 of Part I
-- of the Crimes Act 1958 ... (sexual offences); (c) an offence at common law of rape or assault with intent to rape; (d) an
-- offence against section 41A of the Summary Offences Act 1966 (observation of genital or anal region); (e) ... 21A(1)
-- (stalking), 63 (child stealing) or 63A (kidnapping) ...; (f) ... 77A (home invasion) or 77B (aggravated home invasion)
-- ...; (g) an offence prescribed by the regulations; (h) an offence of conspiracy to commit, incitement to commit or
-- attempting to commit an offence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (g)". Paragraphs (b) and (c) are one choice, "a sexual
-- offence", which is how s 3(1) defines that term.
DECLARE `Kind of offence` IS ONE OF
    `an offence punishable by imprisonment involving assault, injury or a threat of injury to a person`
    `a sexual offence`
    `observation of the genital or anal region`
    `stalking, child stealing or kidnapping`
    `home invasion or aggravated home invasion`
    `an offence the regulations prescribe`
    `a conspiracy, incitement or attempt to commit one of these`
    `none of these`

-- s 3(1) "criminal act means an act or omission by a person that -- (a) constitutes a relevant offence; or (b) would
-- constitute a relevant offence, if the person were not incapable of being criminally responsible ... due to -- (i) age,
-- mental impairment or any other legal incapacity ...; or (ii) the existence of any other lawful defence". The kind of
-- offence is asked as what the act would be, ignoring the offender's age, mental impairment or a defence (para (b)).
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the act is a criminal act` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(1) "act of violence means a criminal act or a series of related criminal acts, committed by one or more persons, that
-- has -- (a) occurred in Victoria; and (b) directly resulted in injury to or the death of one or more persons, regardless of
-- where injury or death occurred". A "means" definition: when it fails, the act is not an act of violence.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it directly resulted in injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the act is an act of violence` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `it directly resulted in injury or death` IF
        `s 3 -- the act is a criminal act` `the offence`
    AND `it occurred in Victoria`
    AND `it directly resulted in injury or death`

-- s 3(1) "injury ... means the following -- (a) actual physical harm; (b) psychological or psychiatric harm; (c)
-- exacerbation of a pre-existing injury ...; (d) any combination ...; (e) any trauma that is -- (i) associated with the act
-- of violence; and (ii) determined by the scheme decision maker to be an injury ... -- but does not include any of the
-- matters ... to the extent that they arise from loss of or damage to property". s 3(3): the determination needs medical or
-- psychological evidence that treatment or counselling is required (asked as the determination itself).
-- "significant adverse effect ... includes any grief, distress, trauma or injury ... as a direct result of the act of
-- violence, but does not include any loss of or damage to property".
DECLARE `Kind of harm` IS ONE OF
    `actual physical harm`
    `psychological or psychiatric harm`
    `an exacerbation of a pre-existing physical, psychological or psychiatric injury`
    `trauma the scheme decision maker has determined to be an injury`
    `trauma not determined to be an injury`
    `grief or distress only`
    `harm arising only from loss of or damage to property`
    `no harm`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the harm is an injury` `the harm` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `actual physical harm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `psychological or psychiatric harm` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an exacerbation of a pre-existing physical, psychological or psychiatric injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `trauma the scheme decision maker has determined to be an injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "includes" grief, distress, trauma or injury: an open list. Property loss is excluded in its own words; "no harm" is no
-- effect at all. Read as closed over the choices offered (fork F2).
GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the harm is a significant adverse effect` `the harm` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `harm arising only from loss of or damage to property` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no harm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 -- primary victims (ss 9, 11)`

-- s 9(1) "A primary victim of an act of violence is a person who is injured or dies as a direct result of an act of
-- violence committed against the person." (2) "... also a primary victim ... if the person is injured or dies as a direct
-- result of trying to -- (a) arrest someone whom the person believes on reasonable grounds has committed an act of
-- violence; or (b) prevent the commission of an act of violence; or (c) aid or rescue someone whom the person believes on
-- reasonable grounds is a victim of an act of violence -- whether or not an act of violence is actually committed." (3) "...
-- if the person -- (a) is injured as a direct result of hearing or witnessing, or otherwise being exposed to the effects
-- of, the act of violence; and (b) is under the age of 18 years at the time ..." (4) "... in a category of persons
-- prescribed by the regulations." (6) "A person is not a primary victim ... if the person committed, and is criminally
-- responsible for, that act of violence."
DECLARE `How I was harmed` IS ONE OF
    `the act of violence was committed against me`
    `trying to arrest someone I believed on reasonable grounds had committed an act of violence`
    `trying to prevent an act of violence`
    `trying to aid or rescue someone I believed on reasonable grounds was a victim of an act of violence`
    `hearing, witnessing or otherwise being exposed to the effects of the act of violence`
    `none of these`

-- A "who is" definition with (4) asked as a fact: closed, so a case in no limb is JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it directly resulted in injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how` IS A `How I was harmed`
      `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
      `the harm was a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was under 18 at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in a prescribed category` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I committed it and am criminally responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 -- I am a primary victim` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `it directly resulted in injury or death` `how` `the harm` `the harm was a direct result` `I was under 18 at the time` `I am in a prescribed category` `I committed it and am criminally responsible` MEANS
    IF `I committed it and am criminally responsible`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `yes or no` (   `s 9(1)` OR `s 9(2)` OR `s 9(3)` OR `I am in a prescribed category`)
    WHERE
        `an act of violence` MEANS `s 3 -- the act is an act of violence` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `it directly resulted in injury or death`
        `injured directly` MEANS `s 3 -- the harm is an injury` `the harm` AND `the harm was a direct result`
        `s 9(1)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how`
            WHEN `the act of violence was committed against me` THEN `an act of violence` AND `injured directly`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `s 9(2)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how`
            WHEN `trying to arrest someone I believed on reasonable grounds had committed an act of violence` THEN `injured directly`
            WHEN `trying to prevent an act of violence` THEN `injured directly`
            WHEN `trying to aid or rescue someone I believed on reasonable grounds was a victim of an act of violence` THEN `injured directly`
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `s 9(3)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how`
            WHEN `hearing, witnessing or otherwise being exposed to the effects of the act of violence` THEN `an act of violence` AND `injured directly` AND `I was under 18 at the time`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 11(1) "A primary victim is eligible for special financial assistance ... if -- (a) either -- (i) an act of violence was
-- committed against the person; or (ii) the person is a primary victim of an act of violence referred to in section 9(3);
-- and (b) the person has experienced or suffered a significant adverse effect as a direct result of that act of violence;
-- and (c) that act of violence is in a category of acts of violence prescribed by the regulations ...". s 9(5) makes a
-- person with a significant adverse effect (and no injury) a primary victim for this purpose only; s 3(4) reads "act of
-- violence" for that person as if they had suffered an injury, so the "resulted in injury" limb of the definition is not
-- asked here (fork F3). s 9(6) still excludes the offender.
-- (2) "The amount ... is -- (a) the minimum amount prescribed by the regulations in relation to the relevant category ... if
-- the scheme decision maker is satisfied that the applicant has experienced or suffered any significant adverse effect
-- ...; and (b) an increased amount up to the maximum amount prescribed ... if the scheme decision maker is satisfied that
-- the applicant has suffered any injury as defined in section 3(1) ...". The regulations (SR 127/2024) are not deposited:
-- the category's minimum and maximum are asked.
DECLARE `Category of act of violence` IS ONE OF
    `category A`
    `category B`
    `category C`
    `category D`
    `not in a prescribed category`

DECLARE `Special financial assistance` IS ONE OF
    `no special financial assistance under s 11`
    `the prescribed minimum for the category` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `from the prescribed minimum up to the prescribed maximum for the category` HAS `at least` IS A NUMBER, `at most` IS A NUMBER
    `eligible, but the decision maker is not yet satisfied of any significant adverse effect`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `committed against me or I was a child exposed to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
      `the harm was a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the category` IS A `Category of act of violence`
      `I committed it and am criminally responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied of a significant adverse effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied of an injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed minimum` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Special financial assistance`
`s 11 -- the special financial assistance I can be paid` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `committed against me or I was a child exposed to it` `the harm` `the harm was a direct result` `the category` `I committed it and am criminally responsible` `satisfied of a significant adverse effect` `satisfied of an injury` `the prescribed minimum` `the prescribed maximum` MEANS
    IF NOT `eligible`
    THEN `no special financial assistance under s 11`
    ELSE IF `satisfied of an injury`
         THEN `from the prescribed minimum up to the prescribed maximum for the category` `the prescribed minimum` `the prescribed maximum`
         ELSE IF `satisfied of a significant adverse effect`
              THEN `the prescribed minimum for the category` `the prescribed minimum`
              ELSE `eligible, but the decision maker is not yet satisfied of any significant adverse effect`
    WHERE
        `in a category` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the category`
            WHEN `not in a prescribed category` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE
        `eligible` MEANS
                (NOT `I committed it and am criminally responsible`)
            AND `s 3 -- the act is a criminal act` `the offence`
            AND `it occurred in Victoria`
            AND `committed against me or I was a child exposed to it`
            AND `s 3 -- the harm is a significant adverse effect` `the harm`
            AND `the harm was a direct result`
            AND `in a category`

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- secondary victims (s 13)`

-- s 13(1) "A secondary victim ... is a person who is present at the scene of an act of violence and who is injured as a
-- direct result of witnessing that act." (2) "... also a secondary victim ... if -- (a) the person is injured as a direct
-- result of subsequently becoming aware of an act of violence; and (b) the person is the parent or guardian of the primary
-- victim ...; and (c) the primary victim was under the age of 18 years at the time ..." (3) "A person is not a secondary
-- victim ... under subsection (2) if the person committed, and is criminally responsible for, that act of violence."
-- s 13(3) reaches subsection (2) only (finding 2); an offender present at the scene is not excluded by s 13 itself.
DECLARE `How I came to know of it` IS ONE OF
    `I was present at the scene and witnessed it`
    `I became aware of it afterwards`
    `neither`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it directly resulted in injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how I knew` IS A `How I came to know of it`
      `the harm` IS A `Kind of harm`
      `the harm was a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a parent or guardian of the primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the primary victim was under 18 at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I committed it and am criminally responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- I am a secondary victim` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `it directly resulted in injury or death` `how I knew` `the harm` `the harm was a direct result` `I am a parent or guardian of the primary victim` `the primary victim was under 18 at the time` `I committed it and am criminally responsible` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`an act of violence` AND `injured directly` AND `a limb holds`)
    WHERE
        `an act of violence` MEANS `s 3 -- the act is an act of violence` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `it directly resulted in injury or death`
        `injured directly` MEANS `s 3 -- the harm is an injury` `the harm` AND `the harm was a direct result`
        `a limb holds` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how I knew`
            WHEN `I was present at the scene and witnessed it` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `I became aware of it afterwards` THEN
                    `I am a parent or guardian of the primary victim`
                AND `the primary victim was under 18 at the time`
                AND (NOT `I committed it and am criminally responsible`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Divisions 3 and 4 -- related victims and funeral expenses (ss 3, 15, 17)`

-- s 3(1) "close family member, in relation to a deceased primary victim, means a person who -- (a) at the time of the
-- victim's death, had a genuine personal relationship with the victim and was also -- (i) the spouse or domestic partner of
-- the victim; or (ii) a parent, guardian or step-parent ...; or (iii) a child or step-child ...; or (iv) a child of whom the
-- victim was the guardian; or (v) a sibling or step-sibling ...; or (b) is a close family member under subsection (2)".
-- s 3(2): "(a) the victim regarded the person as a close family member at the time of the victim's death; and (b) the
-- scheme decision maker considers that it is reasonable to treat the person as a close family member ...".
DECLARE `My relationship to the person who died` IS ONE OF
    `spouse or domestic partner`
    `parent, guardian or step-parent`
    `child or step-child`
    `a child of whom they were the guardian`
    `sibling or step-sibling`
    `another relationship`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `My relationship to the person who died`
      `a genuine personal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they regarded me as a close family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision maker considers it reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- I am a close family member` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship` `they regarded me as a close family member` `the decision maker considers it reasonable` IF
        (`a genuine personal relationship` AND `a listed relationship`)
    OR  (`they regarded me as a close family member` AND `the decision maker considers it reasonable`)
    WHERE
        `a listed relationship` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the relationship`
            WHEN `another relationship` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(1) "dependant ... means -- (a) an individual who -- (i) was wholly or substantially dependent on the victim's income
-- at the time of the victim's death; or (ii) would have been so dependent if not for the victim's incapacity due to the
-- injury from which the person died; or (b) a child of the victim, born after the victim's death, who would have been a
-- dependant under paragraph (a) if born before the victim's death". Asked as one fact covering all three.
--
-- s 15(1) "A related victim of an act of violence is a person who, at the time of the occurrence of the act of violence --
-- (a) was a close family member of; or (b) was a dependant of; or (c) had an intimate personal relationship with -- a
-- primary victim of that act who died as a direct result of that act." (2) "A person is not a related victim ... if the
-- person committed, and is criminally responsible for, that act of violence." "Intimate personal relationship" is not
-- defined: asked. Close family membership is tested at the death (s 3(1)), dependency at the death (s 3(1)), s 15 at the
-- act (finding 3); the facts are asked once, as true at both.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the primary victim died as a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship` IS A `My relationship to the person who died`
      `a genuine personal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they regarded me as a close family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision maker considers it reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was their dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an intimate personal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I committed it and am criminally responsible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- I am a related victim` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `the primary victim died as a direct result` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship` `they regarded me as a close family member` `the decision maker considers it reasonable` `I was their dependant` `an intimate personal relationship` `I committed it and am criminally responsible` MEANS
    IF `I committed it and am criminally responsible`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `yes or no` (    `s 3 -- the act is an act of violence` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `the primary victim died as a direct result`
                      AND `the primary victim died as a direct result`
                      AND (    `s 3 -- I am a close family member` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship` `they regarded me as a close family member` `the decision maker considers it reasonable`
                           OR  `I was their dependant`
                           OR  `an intimate personal relationship`))

-- s 17(1) "A person who has incurred funeral expenses as a direct result of the death of a primary victim of an act of
-- violence may be paid assistance for the funeral expenses actually and reasonably incurred by that person." (2) It is in
-- addition to assistance as a secondary or related victim. A grant limited in its own wording: outside it, NOTHING.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Kind of offence`
      `it occurred in Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the primary victim died as a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I paid or owe funeral expenses for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 -- I may be paid for the funeral expenses` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `the primary victim died as a direct result` `I paid or owe funeral expenses for them` MEANS
    IF     `s 3 -- the act is an act of violence` `the offence` `it occurred in Victoria` `the primary victim died as a direct result`
       AND `the primary victim died as a direct result`
       AND `I paid or owe funeral expenses for them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 17 speaks only of a person who incurred funeral expenses for a primary victim who died)

§§ `Part 2 Division 5 and ss 10, 14, 16, 72 -- how much (ss 10, 14, 16, 18, 19, 37(3))`

-- The Act's own figures, before indexation: s 10(1) "$60 000", s 10(2)(c) "$20 000", s 14(1) "$50 000", s 14(3)(a)
-- "$20 000", s 16(1) "$50 000". Each is "or the higher prescribed amount" and s 72 indexes each from year to year; the
-- Gazette notices are not deposited, so a caller may give the amount in force (0 means the Act's figure).
`s 10(1) -- the Act's maximum for a primary victim` MEANS 60000
`s 10(2)(c) -- the Act's maximum for a primary victim's loss of earnings` MEANS 20000
`s 14(1) -- the Act's maximum for a secondary victim` MEANS 50000
`s 14(3)(a) -- the Act's maximum for a secondary victim's loss of earnings` MEANS 20000
`s 16(1) -- the Act's maximum for a related victim` MEANS 50000

GIVEN `the Act's figure` IS A NUMBER, `the figure in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum from` `the Act's figure` `or` `the figure in force` MEANS
    IF `the figure in force` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the figure in force` ELSE `the Act's figure`

-- s 18(1)(a): the scheme decision maker "must take into account and reduce the amount by the total amount of -- (i) any
-- damages that the person has recovered at common law ...; (ii) any compensation, assistance or payments of any other kind
-- that the person has received ...; (iii) ... financial assistance ... awarded under section 12 of the Transport
-- (Compliance and Miscellaneous) Act 1983 ...", each "for the loss, expense or other matter for which the assistance is
-- sought". (1)(b): "may take into account and reduce the amount by" what the person is likely to recover or receive. (2):
-- for special financial assistance or the s 16(2)(c) distress amount, insurance and superannuation payments must not be
-- taken into account. Read as reducing the amount after the caps are applied (fork F4); the likely amounts are counted only
-- where the decision maker decides to (asked as the amount it takes into account).
DECLARE `What I have received or am likely to receive for the same losses` HAS
    `damages and compensation received, other than insurance or superannuation` IS A NUMBER
    `insurance or superannuation payments received` IS A NUMBER
    `likely amounts the decision maker takes into account, other than insurance or superannuation` IS A NUMBER
    `likely insurance or superannuation payments the decision maker takes into account` IS A NUMBER

-- The reduction under s 18, given the amount within the caps and the part of it that is for distress (which insurance and
-- superannuation cannot reduce).
GIVEN `the amount within the caps` IS A NUMBER
      `the part for distress` IS A NUMBER
      `received` IS A `What I have received or am likely to receive for the same losses`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18 -- the amount after the reductions` `the amount within the caps` `the part for distress` `received` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`the amount within the caps` MINUS `the other reductions` MINUS `the insurance reduction`)
    WHERE
        `the other reductions` MEANS
            `received`'s `damages and compensation received, other than insurance or superannuation`
            PLUS `received`'s `likely amounts the decision maker takes into account, other than insurance or superannuation`
        `the insurance payments` MEANS
            `received`'s `insurance or superannuation payments received`
            PLUS `received`'s `likely insurance or superannuation payments the decision maker takes into account`
        `the insurance reduction` MEANS
            `the lesser of` `the insurance payments` `and` (`not below zero` (`the amount within the caps` MINUS `the part for distress`))

-- s 10(2) "The amount of assistance to a primary victim may be made up of amounts -- (a) for ... reasonable counselling
-- services; and (b) for medical expenses ...; and (c) of up to $20 000 ... for loss of earnings ...; and (d) for ... loss of
-- or damage to clothing worn at the time ...; and (e) for safety-related expenses ...". (3) "In exceptional circumstances,
-- there may also be included ... within the limit set by subsection (1) an amount for other expenses ... to assist the
-- primary victim's recovery". s 19: loss of earnings only for "a period of up to 2 years after the occurrence of the act of
-- violence" (asked as the loss in that period). s 37(3): any interim assistance is deducted.
DECLARE `A primary victim's expenses and losses` HAS
    `counselling` IS A NUMBER
    `medical expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `loss of earnings in the first 2 years` IS A NUMBER
    `clothing lost or damaged` IS A NUMBER
    `safety-related expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `other recovery expenses` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the expenses` IS A `A primary victim's expenses and losses`
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum in force` IS A NUMBER
      `the loss of earnings maximum in force` IS A NUMBER
      `received` IS A `What I have received or am likely to receive for the same losses`
      `interim assistance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10 -- the assistance a primary victim can be paid` `the expenses` `exceptional circumstances` `the maximum in force` `the loss of earnings maximum in force` `received` `interim assistance paid` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`s 18 -- the amount after the reductions` `within the cap` 0 `received` MINUS `interim assistance paid`)
    WHERE
        `the loss of earnings counted` MEANS
            `the lesser of` (`the expenses`'s `loss of earnings in the first 2 years`) `and` (`the maximum from` `s 10(2)(c) -- the Act's maximum for a primary victim's loss of earnings` `or` `the loss of earnings maximum in force`)
        `the other expenses counted` MEANS
            IF `exceptional circumstances` THEN `the expenses`'s `other recovery expenses` ELSE 0
        `the total` MEANS
            `the expenses`'s `counselling`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `medical expenses`
            PLUS `the loss of earnings counted`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `clothing lost or damaged`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `safety-related expenses`
            PLUS `the other expenses counted`
        `within the cap` MEANS
            `the lesser of` `the total` `and` (`the maximum from` `s 10(1) -- the Act's maximum for a primary victim` `or` `the maximum in force`)

-- s 14(2) "(a) for ... reasonable counselling services; and (b) for medical expenses ...". (3) "In exceptional
-- circumstances, there may also be included ... within the limit set by subsection (1) -- (a) an amount of up to $20 000
-- for loss of earnings ...; and (b) an amount for any expenses ... to assist the secondary victim's recovery". (4) nothing
-- for property.
DECLARE `A secondary victim's expenses and losses` HAS
    `counselling` IS A NUMBER
    `medical expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `loss of earnings in the first 2 years` IS A NUMBER
    `other recovery expenses` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the expenses` IS A `A secondary victim's expenses and losses`
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum in force` IS A NUMBER
      `the loss of earnings maximum in force` IS A NUMBER
      `received` IS A `What I have received or am likely to receive for the same losses`
      `interim assistance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14 -- the assistance a secondary victim can be paid` `the expenses` `exceptional circumstances` `the maximum in force` `the loss of earnings maximum in force` `received` `interim assistance paid` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`s 18 -- the amount after the reductions` `within the cap` 0 `received` MINUS `interim assistance paid`)
    WHERE
        `the exceptional amounts` MEANS
            IF `exceptional circumstances`
            THEN (`the lesser of` (`the expenses`'s `loss of earnings in the first 2 years`) `and` (`the maximum from` `s 14(3)(a) -- the Act's maximum for a secondary victim's loss of earnings` `or` `the loss of earnings maximum in force`))
                 PLUS `the expenses`'s `other recovery expenses`
            ELSE 0
        `the total` MEANS
            `the expenses`'s `counselling`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `medical expenses`
            PLUS `the exceptional amounts`
        `within the cap` MEANS
            `the lesser of` `the total` `and` (`the maximum from` `s 14(1) -- the Act's maximum for a secondary victim` `or` `the maximum in force`)

-- s 16(2) "(a) for ... reasonable counselling services; and (b) for medical expenses ...; and (c) for distress experienced,
-- or reasonably likely to be experienced, ... as a direct result of the death ...; and (d) for loss of money that, but for
-- the death ..., the related victim would have been reasonably likely to receive from the primary victim during a period of
-- up to 2 years after that death; and (e) for other expenses ... as a direct result of that death." (3) exceptional
-- circumstances: other recovery expenses, within the limit. s 18(2): insurance and superannuation do not reduce the
-- distress amount; the distress amount is counted first within the cap (fork F4).
DECLARE `A related victim's expenses and losses` HAS
    `counselling` IS A NUMBER
    `medical expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `distress` IS A NUMBER
    `money I would have received from them in the 2 years after the death` IS A NUMBER
    `other expenses from the death` IS A NUMBER
    `other recovery expenses` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the expenses` IS A `A related victim's expenses and losses`
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum in force` IS A NUMBER
      `received` IS A `What I have received or am likely to receive for the same losses`
      `interim assistance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 16 -- the assistance a related victim can be paid` `the expenses` `exceptional circumstances` `the maximum in force` `received` `interim assistance paid` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`s 18 -- the amount after the reductions` `within the cap` (`the lesser of` (`the expenses`'s `distress`) `and` `within the cap`) `received` MINUS `interim assistance paid`)
    WHERE
        `the other expenses counted` MEANS
            IF `exceptional circumstances` THEN `the expenses`'s `other recovery expenses` ELSE 0
        `the total` MEANS
            `the expenses`'s `counselling`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `medical expenses`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `distress`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `money I would have received from them in the 2 years after the death`
            PLUS `the expenses`'s `other expenses from the death`
            PLUS `the other expenses counted`
        `within the cap` MEANS
            `the lesser of` `the total` `and` (`the maximum from` `s 16(1) -- the Act's maximum for a related victim` `or` `the maximum in force`)

§§ `Part 3 Division 1 -- applying (ss 22, 23, 24, 27)`

-- s 22(1)(e): the application "must state whether or not the act of violence has been reported to the police and, if it
-- has not, must be accompanied by a statutory declaration made by the applicant ... setting out -- (i) the circumstances
-- ...; and (ii) the reasons for not reporting the matter". (2) "A statutory declaration under subsection (1)(e) is not
-- required if the applicant is a person in a special reporting category."
GIVEN `it was reported to police` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in a special reporting category` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1)(e), (2) -- I must include a statutory declaration about not reporting` `it was reported to police` `I am in a special reporting category` MEANS
    `yes or no` ((NOT `it was reported to police`) AND (NOT `I am in a special reporting category`))

DECLARE `Who I am applying as` IS ONE OF
    `a primary victim`
    `a secondary victim`
    `a related victim`
    `the person who incurred the funeral expenses`

DECLARE `The time for applying` IS ONE OF
    `at any time` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING
    `by the end of` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE, `the provision` IS A STRING

-- s 23(1) "Subject to this section, an application must be made -- (a) within 3 years after the occurrence of the act of
-- violence; or (b) in the case of an application by a related victim or a person who has incurred funeral expenses, within
-- 3 years after the death of the primary victim." (2) "Subject to subsection (3), an application by or on behalf of a victim
-- who was under the age of 18 years when the act of violence occurred may be made within 3 years after the applicant turns
-- 18 years of age." (3) "... at any time after the occurrence of an act of violence if -- (a) the victim was under the age
-- of 18 years when the act of violence occurred; and (b) the act of violence consisted of or involved child abuse or family
-- violence." (4) "Despite subsection (1), ... within 10 years after the occurrence of an act of violence if -- (a) the
-- victim was at least 18 years old when the act of violence occurred; and (b) the act of violence consisted of or involved a
-- sexual offence or family violence." (5) the regulations may let a victim apply at any time for counselling (asked).
-- (6) a series of related criminal acts "occurs on the occurrence of the last of those criminal acts".
-- (2) to (5) speak of "a victim": the funeral expense payer, not a victim (s 3(1)), has only (1)(b) (finding 4). Where more
-- than one period applies, the latest governs (fork F5). "Within 3 years after" a day ends on its anniversary (fork F1).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who I am applying as`
      `the day of the act` IS A DATE
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `it involved child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved family violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved a sexual offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prescribed counselling circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The time for applying`
`s 23 -- the time for applying` `who` `the day of the act` `the day of the death` `my date of birth` `it involved child abuse` `it involved family violence` `it involved a sexual offence` `a prescribed counselling circumstance applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the person who incurred the funeral expenses` THEN `by the end of` (`the same day` 3 `years after` `the day of the death`) "s 23(1)(b)"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `a child when it occurred` AND (`it involved child abuse` OR `it involved family violence`)
        THEN `at any time` "s 23(3)"
        ELSE IF `a prescribed counselling circumstance applies`
             THEN `at any time` "s 23(5) and the regulations"
             ELSE IF `a child when it occurred`
                  THEN `by the end of` (`the later of` `the s 23(1) day` `and` `the s 23(2) day`) "s 23(1), (2)"
                  ELSE IF `it involved a sexual offence` OR `it involved family violence`
                       THEN `by the end of` (`the later of` `the s 23(1) day` `and` `the s 23(4) day`) "s 23(1), (4)"
                       ELSE `by the end of` `the s 23(1) day` "s 23(1)"
    WHERE
        `a child when it occurred` MEANS `a person born on` `my date of birth` `was under` 18 `on` `the day of the act`
        `the s 23(1) day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who`
            WHEN `a related victim` THEN `the same day` 3 `years after` `the day of the death`
            OTHERWISE `the same day` 3 `years after` `the day of the act`
        `the s 23(2) day` MEANS `the same day` 3 `years after` (`the day a person born on` `my date of birth` `turns` 18)
        `the s 23(4) day` MEANS `the same day` 10 `years after` `the day of the act`

-- The time limit as a rule with a deadline, counted in days from the day of the act (day 0): the applicant DOes the
-- application WITHIN the days to the last day, LEST it is out of time (and s 24 is the only way in). "At any time" has no
-- WITHIN. The "breach" is being out of time, not a wrong.
DECLARE `Applicant` IS ONE OF `the applicant`
DECLARE `Applicant's act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for assistance`
    `respond to the notice of lapse`
    `apply for review`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Applicant` `Applicant's act`
`s 23 -- apply within the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `apply for assistance`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the application was not made within the time in s 23: it can be decided only if the scheme decision maker considers it appropriate under s 24"

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Applicant` `Applicant's act`
`s 23(3), (5) -- apply at any time` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `apply for assistance`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The helper that runs a rule over what happened (as in the County Court Act 1958 and Accident Compensation Act 1985
-- encodings). On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so
-- it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Applicant` `Applicant's act`
      `the act` IS A `Applicant's act`
      `the day it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `done in time under` `the rule` `doing` `the act` `on day` `the day it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day it was done`), (EVENT `the applicant` `the act` `the day it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the time` IS A `The time for applying`
      `the day of the act` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23 -- the application is in time` `the time` `the day of the act` `the day I apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the time`
    WHEN `at any time` p THEN `done in time under` `s 23(3), (5) -- apply at any time` `doing` `apply for assistance` `on day` (`the days from` `the day of the act` `to` `the day I apply`)
    WHEN `by the end of` d p THEN `done in time under` (`s 23 -- apply within the time` (`the days from` `the day of the act` `to` d)) `doing` `apply for assistance` `on day` (`the days from` `the day of the act` `to` `the day I apply`)

-- s 24 "Despite section 23, the scheme decision maker may consider and decide an application made out of time if the scheme
-- decision maker considers that it is appropriate to do so, having regard to [ten matters]". An "if": when the decision
-- maker does not consider it appropriate, the late application is not decided.
DECLARE `Whether my application can be decided` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is in time (s 23)`
    `yes: it is out of time, but the scheme decision maker considers it appropriate to decide it (s 24)`
    `no: it is out of time and the scheme decision maker does not consider it appropriate to decide it (ss 23, 24)`

GIVEN `in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision maker considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my application can be decided`
`ss 23, 24 -- whether the application can be decided` `in time` `the decision maker considers it appropriate` MEANS
    IF `in time`
    THEN `yes: it is in time (s 23)`
    ELSE IF `the decision maker considers it appropriate`
         THEN `yes: it is out of time, but the scheme decision maker considers it appropriate to decide it (s 24)`
         ELSE `no: it is out of time and the scheme decision maker does not consider it appropriate to decide it (ss 23, 24)`

-- s 27(1) "The scheme decision maker may give an applicant written notice that the application will lapse unless the
-- applicant responds to the notice within 6 months." (2) "If the applicant does not respond ... within 6 months after the
-- notice is given, the application lapses at the end of that period." (3) The applicant may reapply, subject to s 23.
-- Counted in days from the day the notice is given (day 0) to the same day 6 months later.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Applicant` `Applicant's act`
`s 27 -- respond to the notice of lapse within 6 months` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `respond to the notice of lapse`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no response within 6 months after the notice was given: the application lapses at the end of that period (s 27(2))"

DECLARE `Where my application stands under s 27` IS ONE OF
    `no notice of lapse has been given: s 27 has not been started`
    `I responded in time: the application does not lapse under s 27`
    `still open: I can still respond` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `lapsed: I may reapply, subject to the time limits in s 23` HAS `the day it lapsed` IS A DATE

GIVEN `a notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `I have responded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I responded` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where my application stands under s 27`
`s 27 -- where my application stands` `a notice was given` `the day the notice was given` `I have responded` `the day I responded` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `a notice was given`
    THEN `no notice of lapse has been given: s 27 has not been started`
    ELSE IF `I have responded`
         THEN IF `done in time under` `the rule` `doing` `respond to the notice of lapse` `on day` (`the days from` `the day the notice was given` `to` `the day I responded`)
              THEN `I responded in time: the application does not lapse under s 27`
              ELSE `lapsed: I may reapply, subject to the time limits in s 23` `the end of the 6 months`
         ELSE IF `done in time under` `the rule` `doing` `respond to the notice of lapse` `on day` (`the days from` `the day the notice was given` `to` `today`)
              THEN `still open: I can still respond` `the end of the 6 months`
              ELSE `lapsed: I may reapply, subject to the time limits in s 23` `the end of the 6 months`
    WHERE
        `the end of the 6 months` MEANS `the same day` 6 `months after` `the day the notice was given`
        `the rule` MEANS `s 27 -- respond to the notice of lapse within 6 months` (`the days from` `the day the notice was given` `to` `the end of the 6 months`)

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- deciding (ss 31, 34(2))`

-- s 31(1) "The scheme decision maker must refuse an application if -- (a) subject to subsection (2), the scheme decision
-- maker is satisfied that -- (i) the act of violence was not reported to the police within a reasonable time; or (ii) the
-- applicant failed to provide reasonable assistance to any person or body duly engaged in the investigation ... or in the
-- arrest or prosecution ...; or (b) the application is made in collusion with the person who committed or is alleged to
-- have committed the act of violence; or (c) an earlier application for assistance by the applicant in any capacity arising
-- from the same act of violence has been made, whether or not the earlier application has been determined." (2) "(1)(a)
-- does not apply if -- (a) the scheme decision maker considers that there were special circumstances for [the late report
-- or the failure] ...; or (b) the applicant is a person in a special reporting category." An "if": when no ground holds,
-- s 31 does not require refusal (JUST FALSE), which is not a decision to pay (s 33 still applies).
GIVEN `satisfied it was not reported within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied I failed to give reasonable assistance to police or prosecutors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in a special reporting category` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made in collusion with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made an earlier application for the same act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31 -- my application must be refused` `satisfied it was not reported within a reasonable time` `satisfied I failed to give reasonable assistance to police or prosecutors` `special circumstances` `I am in a special reporting category` `made in collusion with the offender` `I made an earlier application for the same act` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`paragraph (a)` OR `made in collusion with the offender` OR `I made an earlier application for the same act`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
                (`satisfied it was not reported within a reasonable time` OR `satisfied I failed to give reasonable assistance to police or prosecutors`)
            AND (NOT `special circumstances`)
            AND (NOT `I am in a special reporting category`)

§§ `Part 3 Divisions 3 and 4, Part 5 s 25 -- payment, recognition, representation (ss 25, 36(5), 40)`

-- s 25(2) "A legal practitioner or other person is not entitled to -- (a) charge an applicant, or recover from an applicant,
-- any legal or other costs or amounts for representing or assisting the applicant in relation to the application, except
-- to the extent allowed by the scheme decision maker; or (b) claim a lien ... on any amount of assistance ...; or (c)
-- withhold any legal or other costs or amounts from any amount of assistance ...". (3) despite the Legal Profession Uniform
-- Law. The most is what the decision maker allowed; nothing may be withheld from the assistance.
GIVEN `the amount the decision maker allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 25(2) -- the most my representative may charge me` `the amount the decision maker allowed` MEANS
    `not below zero` `the amount the decision maker allowed`

-- s 36(5) "Any assistance not paid to, or for the benefit of, a person within 10 years after the decision to pay that
-- assistance ceases to be payable unless it is then being held on trust for that person." A period the text fixes: after
-- it, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the day of the decision to pay` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `it is being held on trust for me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(5) -- the unpaid assistance is still payable` `the day of the decision to pay` `today` `it is being held on trust for me` MEANS
    `yes or no` (   `it is being held on trust for me`
                 OR (NOT (`the day` (`the same day` 10 `years after` `the day of the decision to pay`) `is before` `today`)))

-- s 40 "If the scheme decision maker decides to pay assistance to a victim ..., the scheme decision maker must, at the
-- victim's request, give the victim a statement (victim recognition statement) ...". A duty whose "if" is unmet: JUST FALSE
-- (fork F6). The funeral expense payer is not a "victim" (s 3(1)).
GIVEN `the decision maker decided to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a victim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I asked for a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 -- I must be given a victim recognition statement` `the decision maker decided to pay me` `I am a victim` `I asked for a statement` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`the decision maker decided to pay me` AND `I am a victim` AND `I asked for a statement`)

§§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- review (ss 44, 45, 46)`

-- s 44(1) "a reviewable decision is -- (a) any of the following decisions made by the scheme decision maker or a delegate
-- ... -- (i) a refusal of an application for assistance, including a decision to require repayment of any interim
-- assistance; (ii) a decision as to the amount of assistance ...; (iii) a refusal to vary assistance ...; (iv) a decision as
-- to the amount of assistance on an application for variation ...; (v) a decision under Division 3 to require a person to
-- repay an amount of assistance ...; or (b) a decision made by the scheme decision maker on an internal review". (2) a
-- decision about interim assistance "is not a reviewable decision".
-- s 45(1): a reviewable decision "made by a delegate" -- internal review, in writing; (2) "within 28 days after the day on
-- which notice of the reviewable decision, including the reasons ..., is given"; (3) the time may be extended.
-- s 46(1): a reviewable decision "made by the scheme decision maker" -- VCAT; (2) within 28 days after the notice. s 45(5)
-- makes an internal review decision by an appointed member of staff a decision of the scheme decision maker.
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `a refusal of my application, or a requirement to repay interim assistance`
    `the amount of assistance`
    `a refusal to vary my assistance`
    `the amount on my application to vary`
    `a requirement to repay assistance, or the amount to repay`
    `a decision about interim assistance`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `Who made the decision` IS ONE OF
    `a delegate of the scheme decision maker`
    `the scheme decision maker personally`
    `the scheme decision maker on an internal review`

DECLARE `Review open to me` IS ONE OF
    `none: decisions about interim assistance are not reviewable (s 44(2))`
    `none: it is not a reviewable decision (s 44(1))`
    `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `review by VCAT (s 46)` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of decision`
      `who` IS A `Who made the decision`
      `the day I was given notice with reasons` IS A DATE
      `the internal review time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Review open to me`
`ss 44, 45, 46 -- the review open to me` `the kind` `who` `the day I was given notice with reasons` `the internal review time was extended` `the extended last day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the scheme decision maker on an internal review` THEN `review by VCAT (s 46)` `28 days on`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `a decision about interim assistance` THEN `none: decisions about interim assistance are not reviewable (s 44(2))`
        WHEN `another decision` THEN `none: it is not a reviewable decision (s 44(1))`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `who`
            WHEN `a delegate of the scheme decision maker` THEN
                `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` (IF `the internal review time was extended` THEN `the extended last day` ELSE `28 days on`)
            OTHERWISE `review by VCAT (s 46)` `28 days on`
    WHERE
        `28 days on` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I was given notice with reasons`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Applicant` `Applicant's act`
`ss 45(2), 46(2) -- apply for review within the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `apply for review`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no application for review within 28 days after the notice of the decision with reasons (ss 45(2), 46(2)), or within the time as extended (s 45(3))"

-- Whether an application for review made on a day is in time; NOTHING where no review is open.
GIVEN `the review` IS A `Review open to me`
      `the day I was given notice with reasons` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 45, 46 -- my application for review is in time` `the review` `the day I was given notice with reasons` `the day I apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the review`
    WHEN `internal review by the scheme decision maker, applying in writing (s 45)` d THEN JUST (`in time by` d)
    WHEN `review by VCAT (s 46)` d THEN JUST (`in time by` d)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no review is open, so there is no time)
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `in time by` d MEANS
            `done in time under` (`ss 45(2), 46(2) -- apply for review within the time` (`the days from` `the day I was given notice with reasons` `to` d)) `doing` `apply for review` `on day` (`the days from` `the day I was given notice with reasons` `to` `the day I apply`)

§§ `Part 4 Divisions 2 and 3 -- variation and repayment (ss 48, 50)`

DECLARE `The time for applying to vary` IS ONE OF
    `until the last day` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE, `the provision` IS A STRING
    `the longer time the regulations prescribe (s 48(2)(c))`

-- s 48(2) "An application for variation -- (a) subject to paragraphs (b) and (c), must be made within 10 years after the
-- day on which the decision to pay the assistance was made; or (b) subject to paragraph (c), if the person was under the
-- age of 18 years when the decision to pay the assistance was made, may be made at any time until the person turns 28
-- years of age; or (c) may be made within the longer time period prescribed by the regulations ...". "Until the person
-- turns 28": the last day is the day before the 28th birthday (fork F7).
GIVEN `the day of the decision to pay` IS A DATE
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `a longer prescribed period applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The time for applying to vary`
`s 48(2) -- the time for applying to vary` `the day of the decision to pay` `my date of birth` `a longer prescribed period applies` MEANS
    IF `a longer prescribed period applies`
    THEN `the longer time the regulations prescribe (s 48(2)(c))`
    ELSE IF `a person born on` `my date of birth` `was under` 18 `on` `the day of the decision to pay`
         THEN `until the last day` (`the date` (-1) `days after` (`the day a person born on` `my date of birth` `turns` 28)) "s 48(2)(b)"
         ELSE `until the last day` (`the same day` 10 `years after` `the day of the decision to pay`) "s 48(2)(a)"

-- s 50(1)-(2): if after assistance is paid the person receives damages, compensation or other payments "not taken into
-- account ... but which the scheme decision maker would have been required to take into account if received before then",
-- the decision maker "may require the person to repay -- (a) the amount of the assistance ..., if it is equal to or less
-- than the amount ... subsequently received; or (b) the amount ... subsequently received, if the amount of the assistance
-- ... is greater" -- the lesser of the two. (4) If the assistance is decreased on review or variation, the decrease may be
-- required. Both together are read as never more than the assistance paid (fork F8).
GIVEN `the assistance paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments received later that had to be taken into account` IS A NUMBER
      `the decrease on review or variation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 50 -- the most I can be required to repay` `the assistance paid` `the payments received later that had to be taken into account` `the decrease on review or variation` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the assistance paid` `and` (`the lesser of` `the assistance paid` `and` `the payments received later that had to be taken into account` PLUS `the decrease on review or variation`)

§§ `Part 6 s 72 -- indexation of the maximum amounts`

-- s 72(1) "N = P x CPIi / CPIii" (the March-quarter style "last reference period in the previous calendar year" all groups
-- CPI for Melbourne over the same period a year earlier); (2) "made to 4 decimal places but ... rounded to the nearest whole
-- dollar (with a calculation that ends in 5 being rounded up)"; (3) a reduction does not take effect: the amount stays as in
-- the previous year, and next year P is the amount that would have applied but for that. "Made to 4 decimal places" is read
-- as rounding half up to 4 places before the whole-dollar rounding (fork F9).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded half up to 4 decimal places` x MEANS FLOOR ((x TIMES 10000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 10000

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded half up to the whole dollar` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

-- The calculation itself (N), before the no-reduction rule.
GIVEN `P` IS A NUMBER, `CPI i` IS A NUMBER, `CPI ii` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72(1), (2) -- the calculated amount` `P` `CPI i` `CPI ii` MEANS
    `rounded half up to the whole dollar` (`rounded half up to 4 decimal places` ((`P` TIMES `CPI i`) DIVIDED BY `CPI ii`))

-- The amount in force: the calculated amount, unless it is less than last year's actual amount (s 72(3)).
GIVEN `P` IS A NUMBER, `last year's actual amount` IS A NUMBER, `CPI i` IS A NUMBER, `CPI ii` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 72 -- the amount in force this financial year` `P` `last year's actual amount` `CPI i` `CPI ii` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`s 72(1), (2) -- the calculated amount` `P` `CPI i` `CPI ii`) `and` `last year's actual amount`

§§ `Part 7 -- transitional (ss 74, 75)`

-- s 74(2) "An application for variation of an award -- (a) subject to paragraph (b), must be made within 6 years after the
-- day on which the award was originally made under the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1996; or (b) if the person was under
-- the age of 18 years when the award was originally made, may be made at any time until the person turns 24 years of age."
-- (3) "An application for a minor variation may be made more than once but an application for a substantive variation may
-- be made only once." (9) a minor variation gives effect to the award's original intention; any other is substantive.
DECLARE `Kind of variation` IS ONE OF
    `a minor variation, to give effect to the original intention of the award`
    `a substantive variation`

GIVEN `the day the award was originally made` IS A DATE
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of variation`
      `I have already applied for a substantive variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 -- I may apply to vary my Tribunal award` `the day the award was originally made` `my date of birth` `the day I apply` `the kind` `I have already applied for a substantive variation` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`in time` AND `not a second substantive application`)
    WHERE
        `the s 74 last day` MEANS
            IF `a person born on` `my date of birth` `was under` 18 `on` `the day the award was originally made`
            THEN `the date` (-1) `days after` (`the day a person born on` `my date of birth` `turns` 24)
            ELSE `the same day` 6 `years after` `the day the award was originally made`
        `in time` MEANS NOT (`the day` `the s 74 last day` `is before` `the day I apply`)
        `not a second substantive application` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind`
            WHEN `a substantive variation` THEN NOT `I have already applied for a substantive variation`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 75(1) an application may be made under this Act for an act of violence before s 21 commenced (18 November 2024)
-- "unless -- (a) the person received an award before that commencement under the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1996 ...
-- in respect of that act of violence; or (b) the person applied before that commencement for an award ... and that
-- application was refused." (2) a person whose application was pending immediately before commencement may apply "only if
-- -- (a) the person first withdraws their application under the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1996; and (b) no interim
-- award has been made under that Act in relation to the application." (4) "award" excludes an interim award except in
-- (2)(b). Time limits in ss 23, 24 still apply (the note to s 75).
GIVEN `I received an award under the 1996 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my application under the 1996 Act was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my application under the 1996 Act was pending at 18 November 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have withdrawn that application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an interim award was made on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75 -- I may apply under this Act for an act of violence before 18 November 2024` `I received an award under the 1996 Act` `my application under the 1996 Act was refused` `my application under the 1996 Act was pending at 18 November 2024` `I have withdrawn that application` `an interim award was made on it` MEANS
    IF `I received an award under the 1996 Act` OR `my application under the 1996 Act was refused`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `my application under the 1996 Act was pending at 18 November 2024`
         THEN `yes or no` (`I have withdrawn that application` AND (NOT `an interim award was made on it`))
         ELSE JUST TRUE
